    <string name="instructions_title">How to use WorkBalance</string>
    <string name="instruction_1_title">1. Check-in and check-out</string>
    <string name="instruction_1_body">Tap “Check in” when you enter the workplace and “Check out” whenever you leave. A later check-in continues the same day.</string>
    <string name="instruction_2_title">2. Break</string>
    <string name="instruction_2_body">Off-site time first covers the required break. If the off-site intervals are shorter, the missing part is deducted from on-site time. Any time beyond the required break is shown as additional absence.</string>
    <string name="instruction_3_title">3. Correcting records</string>
    <string name="instruction_3_body">Tap a record on the Today screen or select a day in the calendar. You can change its time, delete a mistake, or add a missing interval.</string>
    <string name="instruction_4_title">4. Balance</string>
    <string name="instruction_4_body">“Balance before today” is the sum of previous days. The red hint shows the current deficit including today and how long you need to stay to clear it.</string>
    <string name="instruction_5_title">5. Monthly plan</string>
    <string name="instruction_5_body">In the calendar, mark a day as “Unavailable — make up in advance”. Its target remains in the monthly plan, but the required hours are distributed across available days.</string>
    <string name="instruction_6_title">6. Forgotten records</string>
    <string name="instruction_6_body">Enable check-in and check-out reminders in Settings. A notification can create the record now, snooze the reminder, or mark today as unavailable. Location is never used.</string>
    <string name="instruction_7_title">7. Backup</string>
    <string name="instruction_7_body">Save a JSON backup before updating or moving to another phone. CSV is intended for comparing the selected month with an access-control report.</string>
    <string name="instruction_8_title">8. Production calendar</string>
    <string name="instruction_8_body">Russian public holidays, regional holidays, and shortened days can be enabled separately. In “Ask” mode, your answer is saved for that date. A manually selected day type always has priority.</string>
    <string name="instruction_9_title">9. Quick access</string>
    <string name="instruction_9_body">Add the home-screen widget or the WorkBalance Quick Settings tile. Every button uses the same local database.</string>
    <string name="instruction_10_title">10. Updates</string>
    <string name="instruction_10_body">Open GitHub or check for a new version in About. Automatic checks run at startup no more than once a day and never send work records.</string>
